From 6e8fe143b79abee101df242287b7d6513c5d8833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:17:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] VPN: a stock provider row no longer switches a client; IPsec
 profile checks

- vpn_utils.c: on this build the stock VPN Fusion list is not the source of truth. A provider row
  kept from the stock firmware switched its WireGuard or OpenVPN client off (or on) at every boot,
  which read as a lost key. The list no longer sets a client's switch; the VPN Client page says
  whether a WireGuard key is saved.
- IPsec: every saved profile is checked before ipsec.secrets and the strongSwan configuration are
  written (control characters, one-token fields, Instant Guard names, subnets); a newly refused
  profile's tunnel goes down; an IPv6 local subnet is kept; the export no longer stops on a subnet
  without a prefix length. The WAN address check before the server certificate runs with its
  arguments in the right order. A VPN server subnet that is not three octets is skipped
  (mtlan_utils.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
